                    "Net Influencer this morning, reading a Financial Times report: Sekura Asset Management began lending to creators this year and managing partner Samuel Oiknine expects the book to reach <mark>100 million dollars in 2027</mark>.  About <mark>two thirds of its creator financing goes to YouTube creators</mark>, the rest split across TikTok, Instagram and Twitch.  Minimum requirement is 1 million dollars of annual creator revenue, individual deals were previously capped at 2 million, and a new fund with the Swiss firm Copyright Capital lets it write larger ones.",
